    {
      "id": "ev_44",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "NAOUK_Investigation-WannaCry-cyber-attack-and-the-NHS(10-27-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 16,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p16_s1"
      },
      "text": "If the WannaCry ransomware attack had led to any patient harm or loss of data then NHS England told us that it would expect trusts to report cases through existing reporting channels, such as reporting data loss direct to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) in line with existing policy and guidance on information governance.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_51",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "NAOUK_Investigation-WannaCry-cyber-attack-and-the-NHS(10-27-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 17,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p17_s4"
      },
      "text": "This meant that some NHS organisations were infected by the WannaCry malware, but because of the actions of the researcher they were not locked out of their devices and systems.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_54",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "NAOUK_Investigation-WannaCry-cyber-attack-and-the-NHS(10-27-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 18,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p18_s1"
      },
      "text": "• 37 trusts infected by the WannaCry malware; and • 44 trusts not infected by the malware but reporting disruption.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_59",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "NAOUK_Investigation-WannaCry-cyber-attack-and-the-NHS(10-27-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 20,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p20_s4"
      },
      "text": "2.7 The Department and Cabinet Office had written to trusts in 2014 offering some temporary help with security for old equipment until April 2015, after which time there would be no support.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_65",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "NAOUK_Investigation-WannaCry-cyber-attack-and-the-NHS(10-27-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 21,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p21_s1"
      },
      "text": "• WannaCry exploited weaknesses within parts of Microsoft’s Windows operating system used to share files within organisations.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_73",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "NAOUK_Investigation-WannaCry-cyber-attack-and-the-NHS(10-27-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 24,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p24_s1"
      },
      "text": "Coordinates public communications in agreement with other organisations Cabinet Office leads on (non-mandatory) policies and principles, although all departments and bodies are accountable and responsible for their own cyber-security",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
